1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:36,310
Oh, they're not dead. Looks like they're just paralyzed.

2
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:39,430
Must have been those things. Can you heal them?

3
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:40,310
I'll see.

4
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:53,450
Well, I hope you had a decent nap.

5
00:01:53,450 --> 00:02:00,450
What happened? Did we get wiped out?

6
00:02:00,730 --> 00:02:02,670
Wait, where's my necklace?

7
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:04,930
Damn it! My coins are gone too!

8
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:07,250
I can't find any of the jewels either.

9
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:09,890
Some of our belongings have gone missing.

10
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,470
Did you see what happened?

11
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:14,490
There's no doubt. Treasure insects.

12
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:17,130
Shh! Sorry, couldn't tell you.

13
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:20,810
When we got here, you guys were just laying by the wall all lined up.

14
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:24,250
So I'm willing to bet that someone came here before we did.

15
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:26,570
This is hair.

16
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:29,410
It's used to repel ghosts.

17
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,390
Apparently, there was someone else who found us.

18
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:33,170
Hmm.

19
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:36,030
Elf.

20
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:38,350
A tall man.

21
00:02:39,090 --> 00:02:40,230
Half foot.

22
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,870
A dwarf, too.

23
00:02:42,790 --> 00:02:44,750
They ate a meal in this exact spot.

24
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:45,890
They what?

25
00:02:46,350 --> 00:02:48,030
Who would have the nerve to do that?

26
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:49,190
Come on!

27
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,070
Not so fast.

28
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:53,210
This ain't a charity.

29
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:56,810
Here.

30
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:58,270
Thanks, kid.

31
00:03:00,770 --> 00:03:02,790
Why didn't you just tell him the truth?

32
00:03:03,190 --> 00:03:04,170
Why should I?

33
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:07,150
More corpses means more money, after all.

34
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:14,550
I hope I can wash my hair soon.

35
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:16,790
Save the trouble and shave it off.

36
00:03:17,110 --> 00:03:19,410
You really don't have to be so mean to me, you know.

37
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:22,170
Bet you really want to wash your beard, right, Senshi?

38
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:26,390
You don't even comb that thing, do you?

39
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:27,770
We need to clean it now.

40
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:31,150
Hair is actually pretty important for magic.

41
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:35,130
Taking care of it is kind of like doing warm-up exercises.

42
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:39,230
If your beard's dirty, then my support magic might not work on you.

43
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:40,750
That's fine by me.

44
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:44,450
Oh, I just remembered I have some good soap with me.

45
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:47,450
Let's wash your beard with that and braid it after.

46
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:50,170
Hmm?

47
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:52,250
Uh, where is it?

48
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:53,390
Ah!

49
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:57,010
Back then, it must have...

50
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:58,150
It's all gone!

51
00:03:58,270 --> 00:03:59,570
It got so much money!

52
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:00,570
Let's go.

53
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:03,850
The fourth floor.

54
00:04:04,570 --> 00:04:07,510
Underground water rushes out of holes in the bedrock,

55
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:09,450
forming a large lake.

56
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:13,490
The water is imbued with magic and glows faintly.

57
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:16,750
At the bottom of the lake, you can see the castle town,

58
00:04:17,150 --> 00:04:18,670
rippling like a mirage.

59
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:22,870
Hey, Senshi, what exactly do you do when you're exploring this floor?

60
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:26,290
I usually just fish or lay traps all around this area.

61
00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:27,750
That's about it.

62
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:30,470
How do you folks get past this point?

63
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:32,350
Isn't it obvious?

64
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:33,930
Magic, of course.

65
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:34,950
Check it out.

66
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,310
First, I do this.

67
00:04:40,390 --> 00:04:42,490
And then we just walk across the water.

68
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:46,330
No!

69
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:49,810
No, no, no, no, no!

70
00:04:50,030 --> 00:04:51,710
You don't have to throw such a fit.

71
00:04:51,710 --> 00:04:52,630
I don't think you can make me!

72
00:04:52,650 --> 00:04:53,550
This isn't gonna work.

73
00:04:53,970 --> 00:04:55,310
Tie him up and pull him along.

74
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:56,930
Marcel?

75
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:59,530
Go ahead and cast your spell while I hold him down!

76
00:04:59,810 --> 00:05:00,110
Huh?

77
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:00,930
Hurry!

78
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:04,770
Senshi, this is the only way to do it, wearing armor!

79
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:06,830
The boat is too risky!

80
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:07,310
Cut!

81
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:10,550
People are so quick to give in to the simple path.

82
00:05:10,930 --> 00:05:14,730
It only takes a second to rust, but to sharpen it takes a long time!

83
00:05:14,730 --> 00:05:18,910
You see, that didn't kill you, did it?

84
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:20,630
Why, you little...

85
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:22,310
I honestly don't get it.

86
00:05:22,470 --> 00:05:23,970
Why are you so opposed to magic?

87
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:25,970
You wanna know what I don't get?

88
00:05:26,170 --> 00:05:28,830
How you lot can throw around spells all willy-nilly.

89
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:29,790
It's careless.

90
00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:31,670
Hey, come on.

91
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:33,170
What's done is done, isn't it?

92
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:34,430
Who knows?

93
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:35,770
You might even end up...

94
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:36,190
...liking it!

95
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:40,010
Huh?

96
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:42,190
Wait, what?

97
00:05:42,430 --> 00:05:43,890
Why is the spell so ineffective?

98
00:05:44,570 --> 00:05:47,490
Is it because maybe his hair works as an insulator?

99
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:50,910
Seems likely with all this monster blood and oil kicked in...

100
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:51,310
Seriously?

101
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:53,270
Wash that gross thing already!

102
00:05:53,590 --> 00:05:55,210
It'll take much more than water.

103
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:56,090
There's no need.

104
00:05:57,170 --> 00:05:58,390
Don't worry about me.

105
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,370
I'll cross the lake my own way.

106
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:03,070
You gonna make a boat?

107
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:04,990
He'll just sink like a stone.

108
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:05,730
Hold on.

109
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:08,210
I bet whatever idea he came up with is awesome.

110
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:10,370
What's with the sudden, unwavering faith?

111
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:11,950
He must be losing it.

112
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:13,270
Just watch.

113
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:16,970
The shell of a mimic?

114
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:17,670
Shh!

115
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,390
Oh.

116
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:32,630
Kelby!

117
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,110
Careful!

118
00:06:33,450 --> 00:06:34,310
It's getting closer!

119
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:35,470
Calm down.

120
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:36,450
She's harmless.

121
00:06:37,590 --> 00:06:40,810
Anne here often comes to visit me when I'm trying to catch fish.

122
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:41,850
You named it?

123
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:46,110
I've always been curious about whether or not I could cross the lake with her.

124
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:52,210
Maybe I can use a mimic shell as bait to help lead her over to the other side.

125
00:06:52,590 --> 00:06:52,890
Really?

126
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:54,310
That would be...

127
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:56,650
...absolutely incredible!

128
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:57,650
I'm against this.

129
00:06:57,650 --> 00:06:58,810
I'm against this.

130
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:03,590
If we used its organs as a life preserver, it'd be more useful.

131
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:05,550
That's awful!

132
00:07:05,950 --> 00:07:07,630
I can't believe you just said that.

133
00:07:08,450 --> 00:07:09,990
All monsters are dangerous.

134
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:11,790
Friendly ones are no exception.

135
00:07:12,990 --> 00:07:15,970
Kelpies try to lower your guard to coax you into the water.

136
00:07:16,650 --> 00:07:18,910
You never know a monster's true intentions.

137
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:22,530
Look, I've known Anne for just as long as I've known the golems.

138
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:25,190
So don't try and tell me I don't know her.

139
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:33,050
Why are people so soft when it comes to mammals, yet they're totally against growing man-eating plants?

140
00:07:33,730 --> 00:07:36,130
Uh, do you really need me to explain it?

141
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:37,750
All right, Anne.

142
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:38,530
Let's go.

143
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:44,850
Sanshi!

144
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:46,170
Here, catch!

145
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:55,810
Anne.

146
00:08:02,810 --> 00:08:03,850
Stop it, Anne.

147
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:30,670
You can't die!

148
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:30,730
You can't die!

149
00:08:30,730 --> 00:08:34,730
You can't die!

150
00:08:34,730 --> 00:08:41,130
So she was just waiting for me to get on her back?

151
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:42,250
Why?

152
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:43,850
She could have attacked whenever.

153
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:45,090
Yeah.

154
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:48,930
I can't even begin to understand how monsters think.

155
00:08:50,090 --> 00:08:51,250
I don't get it.

156
00:08:52,210 --> 00:08:53,790
I don't get it one bit.

157
00:08:57,390 --> 00:08:58,110
Hey.

158
00:08:58,790 --> 00:08:59,950
Aren't you freezing?

159
00:09:00,490 --> 00:09:02,270
I could start a fire.

160
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:04,170
Wait.

161
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:07,630
You loved her so much, but you're going to eat her?

162
00:09:08,430 --> 00:09:09,930
I can't believe it.

163
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:11,210
Why do this?

164
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:12,850
Need a hand?

165
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:14,870
No.

166
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,410
I'm doing this alone.

167
00:09:17,410 --> 00:09:18,410
I'm doing this alone.

168
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:19,310
I'm doing this alone.

169
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:19,370
Hmm.

170
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:24,930
Hey.

171
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:29,090
If it's no trouble, could I have a little bit of the fat?

172
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:31,670
Weren't you opposed to me doing this?

173
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,670
I was.

174
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:38,670
I was, but...

175
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:41,190
Seriously.

176
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:43,330
What did we even come here for?

177
00:09:43,990 --> 00:09:44,470
Chill, Chuck.

178
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:45,050
Huh?

179
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:49,090
There's something floating over there, and I'm worried it's people.

180
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:50,090
Let's go.

181
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:52,410
Do we have to?

182
00:09:52,410 --> 00:09:58,510
What are these little white things?

183
00:09:58,950 --> 00:09:59,430
Barley.

184
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:01,390
Must be leaking from a bag.

185
00:10:01,570 --> 00:10:03,230
Well, I found the owners.

186
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:04,150
Yeah.

187
00:10:05,030 --> 00:10:06,550
Let's get them back to land.

188
00:10:06,890 --> 00:10:07,010
Huh?

189
00:10:07,490 --> 00:10:08,190
What's wrong?

190
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:09,630
He looks familiar.

191
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:11,250
Have we seen this guy before?

192
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:12,150
Nope.

193
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:14,890
Oh, I remember this kobold.

194
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:17,310
We saw him knocked out on the third floor, too.

195
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:19,570
How'd these guys get ahead of us?

196
00:10:19,570 --> 00:10:20,570
Jeez.

197
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:27,290
Jeez.

198
00:10:27,770 --> 00:10:28,990
They fought fishmen, huh?

199
00:10:29,570 --> 00:10:30,610
That's unlucky.

200
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:34,750
Uh-huh.

201
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:36,550
Chill, Chuck?

202
00:10:37,450 --> 00:10:38,170
Hey!

203
00:10:38,950 --> 00:10:39,650
Chill, Chuck!

204
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:42,770
Stop!

205
00:10:42,770 --> 00:10:42,830
Stop!

206
00:10:49,570 --> 00:11:18,290
I didn't get to finish singing it again.

207
00:11:18,290 --> 00:11:19,850
I even learned it all, too.

208
00:11:20,290 --> 00:11:20,810
Oh.

209
00:11:22,570 --> 00:11:25,150
I think that should do it.

210
00:11:26,250 --> 00:11:28,430
I feel bad that their barley's scattered.

211
00:11:29,110 --> 00:11:29,890
Should we help them?

212
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:32,030
I doubt they would still want it.

213
00:11:32,270 --> 00:11:33,510
Then let's take it with us.

214
00:11:34,190 --> 00:11:35,310
It'll make Marcelle happy.

215
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:37,410
No, I don't think it will.

216
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:37,910
Huh?

217
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:43,550
No way!

218
00:11:44,330 --> 00:11:45,890
I didn't say anything yet.

219
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,630
We all agreed that demi-humans are off limits, remember?

220
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:51,470
Okay, but think about it.

221
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:53,830
What are demi-humans?

222
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:54,890
What'd you just say?

223
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:57,110
There are different types of mermaids.

224
00:11:57,370 --> 00:11:58,930
The mammal type and the fish type.

225
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:00,770
This is the fish type.

226
00:12:00,770 --> 00:12:04,350
It has gills and lays eggs, so there's no belly button or nipples.

227
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:08,430
Classification-wise, they're farther from humans than cows or pigs.

228
00:12:11,750 --> 00:12:12,690
Dylan, no!

229
00:12:14,290 --> 00:12:15,750
Tell me what's wrong with it!

230
00:12:15,990 --> 00:12:18,510
Why is a cow okay, but a fish man somehow isn't?

231
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:20,470
It just doesn't feel right to me, okay?

232
00:12:20,910 --> 00:12:21,850
Feel right?

233
00:12:23,790 --> 00:12:24,510
Feelings, huh?

234
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:29,790
They're still going at it.

235
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:32,650
I'm hungry, so let's start making something to eat.

236
00:12:33,870 --> 00:12:36,030
Soak the barley and put it over a flame.

237
00:12:36,550 --> 00:12:38,970
Pull apart some mimic meat and add a few water plants.

238
00:12:39,310 --> 00:12:40,390
Hold on a second.

239
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:42,550
Wasn't that growing out of the fish man's head?

240
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:46,170
I mean, yes, but this is also a completely ordinary plant.

241
00:12:46,610 --> 00:12:48,590
Fish men use these to mimic the mermaids.

242
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:51,670
Without it, they would probably look a lot more like fish.

243
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:55,170
Fish, you're not going to let me eat it, are you?

244
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:57,290
Here we go again.

245
00:12:57,970 --> 00:12:59,050
All right, whatever.

246
00:12:59,350 --> 00:13:00,210
Do what you want.

247
00:13:02,470 --> 00:13:05,450
Why do I get the feeling that I just made a huge mistake?

248
00:13:06,210 --> 00:13:07,990
All right, it's ready.

249
00:13:10,470 --> 00:13:11,570
Come on, you two.

250
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,790
Time for lunch.

251
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:14,470
Is it that time already?

252
00:13:15,130 --> 00:13:17,370
Hey, where did you get this barley from?

253
00:13:17,810 --> 00:13:20,230
It was near some dead adventurers, so he nabbed it.

254
00:13:20,230 --> 00:13:21,650
What were you thinking?

255
00:13:23,090 --> 00:13:25,470
Yeah, we probably shouldn't have done that.

256
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:27,210
Well, it's already cooked.

257
00:13:27,310 --> 00:13:28,090
It doesn't matter.

258
00:13:28,650 --> 00:13:30,130
Thanks a lot for making lunch.

259
00:13:38,570 --> 00:13:40,110
Something's popping in my mouth.

260
00:13:40,310 --> 00:13:41,270
I wonder what that is.

261
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:42,250
Fish eggs, maybe?

262
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:44,590
They might have been stuck in the water plants.

263
00:13:44,590 --> 00:13:46,890
Mmm, it's tasty.

264
00:13:47,170 --> 00:13:48,550
Yeah, it is, isn't it?

265
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:50,350
Glad I put them in.

266
00:13:51,050 --> 00:13:51,930
Can we talk?

267
00:13:52,810 --> 00:13:55,810
Hey, those were the fish men's eggs, weren't they?

268
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:58,450
I heard that they lay eggs and hide them in water plants.

269
00:13:58,850 --> 00:14:01,290
Specifically the ones that are growing straight out of their heads.

270
00:14:02,010 --> 00:14:02,830
Everything good?

271
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:04,530
Depends.

272
00:14:04,530 --> 00:14:08,530
Does that taste okay?

273
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:10,150
Hmm.

274
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:12,510
Sure does!

275
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:18,630
Senshi?

276
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:21,290
This is for you.

277
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:22,090
Hmm?

278
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:25,250
I made some soap from the kelpie fat you gave me.

279
